  "editorial_note": "GitHub listed only ten projects this Thursday morning, and six of them were featured here in the past week. Today's four picks are all first appearances: OpenAI's ==Codex Security scanner, which shipped version 0.10.0 overnight==, Google Chrome's Modern Web Guidance skills for coding agents, shadcn's improve skill that ==plans with an expensive model and executes with a cheap one==, and The Algorithms' long-running Java collection. Curation order reflects practical interest, not GitHub rank. Trending is not a release date or an endorsement.",
  "coverage_notes": [
    "GitHub's daily listing held only 10 rows at capture, the shortest list of the past week (9 to 18 rows from 5 to 11 November). The capture parsed exactly ten listing rows and is GitHub's own list, not a truncation by us.",
    "All 10 listing entries were inspected. Exact public GitHub API metadata was checked at about 07:01:21 UTC for every candidate, and recent releases for every entry; README files of the four picks were read at about 07:01:27 UTC. Every checked repository was active and unarchived.",
    "Six entries featured in the past seven days were left out without a new primary-sourced reason: meta/astryx (8 November), homeassistant-ai/ha-mcp, vercel-labs/agent-browser and ZhuLinsen/daily_stock_analysis (10 November), and addyosmani/agent-skills and we-promise/sure (11 November).",
    "meta/astryx shipped v0.7.14 on 11 November; its notes describe component behaviour changes (touch-press menus, anchored-layer animation, segmented-control drags), which we did not judge a material change since the 8 November pick. homeassistant-ai/ha-mcp's new releases since 10 November are dev builds (v9.3.0.dev*), also not judged material.",
    "The preceding seven calendar dates, 5-11 November, were checked for local history; all seven editions exist.",
    "The official listing was captured at 08:01:09 Europe/Paris. Literal stars-today labels are GitHub's displayed period figures; API total stars and README evidence were checked separately at the times shown per card. They are not an independently audited rolling 24-hour growth measurement.",
    "Feature descriptions and eval figures come from each project's own README and release notes and are the maintainers' claims. No candidate code, installer, CLI, plugin, skill or model was installed, downloaded or run, and none of this is a security audit or endorsement."
  ],
