      "readme_source_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex-security/readme",
      "evidence_urls": [
        "https://github.com/openai/codex-security",
        "https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex-security",
        "https://github.com/openai/codex-security/releases/tag/npm-v0.10.0"
      ],
      "description": "Codex Security is ==OpenAI's CLI and TypeScript SDK for finding, validating and patching vulnerabilities== with Codex models. It scans a repository, selected paths or a Git diff, saves a report with findings and a threat model, drafts SECURITY.md policies, exports SARIF, JSON and CSV, and ships a GitHub Action for scheduled scans.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. It goes past flagging issues: ==validate a finding, generate a patch, then verify the fix==. Version 0.10.0, published about five hours before our capture, adds resumable Standard scans, a shared cost budget across batch scans and clearer reports when a patch is blocked; the README says scans also run through Amazon Bedrock, OpenRouter and Fireworks AI.",
      "caveat": "Scans are ==paid model calls sent to an AI provider==: the README's example Action sets an estimated $5 limit per scan and warns in-flight requests can exceed it, and 0.10.0 carries breaking changes to paths and MCP setup. It needs a login or API key, some protected findings require OpenAI's Trusted Access for Cyber, and it is for code you are authorised to test. We did not run it."
    },
