      "readme_source_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/GoogleChrome/modern-web-guidance-src/readme",
      "evidence_urls": [
        "https://github.com/GoogleChrome/modern-web-guidance-src",
        "https://api.github.com/repos/GoogleChrome/modern-web-guidance-src",
        "https://github.com/GoogleChrome/modern-web-guidance",
        "https://developer.chrome.com/docs/modern-web-guidance"
      ],
      "description": "This is the source repository for Modern Web Guidance, ==a skill and CLI that feed coding agents current web-platform patterns==: View Transitions, container queries, the Popover API, scheduler.yield and some 250 features in all. The agent searches the guides locally and pulls one targeted guide, with fallbacks and Baseline browser-support data, into its context.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. The README says it is stewarded by the Chrome, Edge, Firefox and MDN teams, and it targets a real failure: agents ==defaulting to legacy JavaScript where a native API now exists==. Its eval harness grades agents with and without the guidance on Playwright-checked tasks; the maintainers report 27 to 36 point pass-rate gains in November runs.",
      "caveat": "The eval gains are the maintainers' own figures on their own test apps, not an independent benchmark. The CLI ==sends anonymous usage telemetry, including agent search queries, to Google== unless DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1 is set, and the guide text is CC-BY 4.0 while the code is Apache-2.0. Install it from the published GoogleChrome/modern-web-guidance package, not this source repo. We did not install it."
    },
    {
      "repository": "shadcn/improve",
      "url": "https://github.com/shadcn/improve",
      "trending_rank": 4,
      "category": "AI agents / code audit",
