      "readme_source_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/shadcn/improve/readme",
      "evidence_urls": [
        "https://github.com/shadcn/improve",
        "https://api.github.com/repos/shadcn/improve"
      ],
      "description": "improve is ==an agent skill that audits a codebase and writes implementation plans== instead of code. A /improve run maps the repo, fans out subagents across nine categories from correctness to direction, re-checks each cited file and line, and writes one self-contained plan per chosen finding into plans/, with verification commands and stop conditions.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. It encodes a cost pattern many teams improvise: ==spend the strong model on judgement, hand execution to cheaper models==. Plans are plain Markdown any agent or human can pick up, an execute mode reviews a cheaper model's diff in an isolated worktree, and a reconcile mode retires findings that were fixed elsewhere.",
      "caveat": "A full audit with parallel subagents on your most capable model ==can cost real tokens==, so the README offers a cheaper quick pass. Its read-only and no-secrets rules are instructions to the agent, not enforced sandboxing. The repository was last pushed on 12 September 2026 and has no releases, so it is a prompt pack to read before installing. We did not install it."
    },
