      "description": "The Algorithms - Java is ==a community collection of classic algorithms and data structures written in Java==, from sorting and graphs to conversions and ciphers, indexed in a DIRECTORY.md file and built with Maven, with checkstyle, PMD and SpotBugs configured in the repository.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list, and the one non-agent pick today. Running since 2016 and still merging fixes this week (a hex-to-octal input check on 11 November), it is ==a readable reference for interview prep and teaching==, where each algorithm sits in plain Java you can step through.",
      "caveat": "The README says the code is ==for learning, and may be less efficient than the Java standard library==; use library or well-tested implementations in production. Quality varies across many contributors, and Trending is no sign of anything new here. We did not run it."
